# Security Mandate (Always Apply)

Before writing or reviewing backend API or frontend/client code, read and follow **[SECURITY.md](../../SECURITY.md)** in full.

## Non-negotiable rules

1. **Zero-trust auth** — global JWT guard; only `@Public()` routes skip authentication.
2. **BOLA/IDOR** — verify resource ownership and `tenantId` scope on every read/write by ID.
3. **Strict validation** — DTO + `ValidationPipe` (`whitelist`, `forbidNonWhitelisted`, `transform`); reject unknown fields.
4. **Secure tokens** — httpOnly cookies only; no JWT in `localStorage`; rotate refresh tokens; revoke all sessions on reuse.
5. **Rate limits** — protect login, OTP, public forms, uploads, webhooks.
6. **No PII in logs** — never log passwords, tokens, OTP, API keys, identity numbers.
7. **Webhooks** — signature verify on raw body; idempotency on money paths.
8. **No shadow APIs** — no unauthenticated or undocumented endpoints.

## Before finishing any task

Complete the checklist in SECURITY.md §12. Fix issues at the shared guard/service layer. Do not leave known vulnerabilities in the diff.

Also follow [PERFORMANCE.md](../../PERFORMANCE.md) for query and pagination rules.
